<%# locals: (form:, hint_id: nil, autofocus: false) %>
<%#
  030 FR-004: the one floor control every floor entry form renders — the user's
  own locker profile (first entry and pencil editor), the locker wish's declare
  and "Change floor" forms, and an administrator's editor for another account.
  One definition, so the three cannot drift apart. The label, the hint and the
  field wrapper stay with each caller, which is where they differ.

  FR-006: until the super admin saves a list, this is exactly the text field it
  always was. Once one is saved it becomes a <select> of the listed floors, in
  the order typed (clarification Q3). 017 ruled a <select> out for the floor
  *filters*, because one that submits on change fires as a keyboard user arrows
  through it; this one sits inside a form with its own submit, so moving through
  it commits nothing (research.md R6).

  FR-007: a record already on a floor that has since left the list keeps it —
  it is offered, selected, and marked as no longer offered, so the person sees
  what is on file and can save the form without being made to move. Read from
  the saved value, so a rejected edit being corrected does not invent one.

  The list is read once, here, rather than once per question asked of it.
%>
<% floor_list = SiteFloorList.current %>

<% if floor_list.configured? %>
  <% options = floor_list.floors.map { |floor| [ floor, floor ] } %>
  <% saved_floor = form.object.saved_floor %>
  <% if saved_floor.present? && !floor_list.offers?(saved_floor) %>
    <% options.unshift([ t("shared.floor_field.no_longer_offered", floor: saved_floor), saved_floor ]) %>
  <% end %>

  <%= form.select :floor, options,
        { include_blank: t("shared.floor_field.prompt") },
        { autofocus: autofocus, aria: { describedby: hint_id }.compact, class: "field-input" } %>
<% else %>
  <%= form.text_field :floor, autofocus: autofocus, autocomplete: "off",
        aria: { describedby: hint_id }.compact, class: "field-input" %>
<% end %>
